A||||7||88formula||Header wrap||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||04-01-2000||10:42 PM||||Would you guys use header wrap on the stock fiero manifolds? Will this wrap cause problems like cracking?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DiggityDan||04-01-2000||10:52 PM||||With my experience with turbo breathing cars..headerwrap is very bad. The liquid coatings work really well, but you must have the inside done as well or you will notice the same problems as with the wraps. As a side note, using wrap at the track for limited use is a very productive trick....just don't drive around with it all the time||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||04-01-2000||11:01 PM||||That's what I thought. thanks DiggityDan.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||04-02-2000||01:14 PM||||I've had my stock manifolds and Y-pipe wraped with the Thermo-TEC ceramic tape since June... used stailness hose clamps to hold it on. I've gone through 16 bottles of nitrous, 4 clutches and 2 sets of rear tires and the manifolds and y-pipe are fine. I'm actually gunna sell them once the new headers are on my car... They are being sent to Jet-HOT for a ceramic thermal protective coating. No cracking problems, no mis alignment problems.. nothing. Just that caraimc crap in your hands when you work on the car with out glove.. that my only complaint.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-02-2000||01:19 PM||||oh and for turbo car... they are dealing with the same heat I am with the nitrous on.. (STUPID HIGH EGTs) the shop that suggested I do this build 10sec starions, Civics and such nearly EVERY car they have come out of their shop has either a Ceramic coating or Thermo-TEC ceramic tape... just depends on the owners budget and what he/she is shooting for.  <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||04-02-2000||01:28 PM||||Hoew many hours do you run your car at a time and how many overall since the wrap?||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||04-02-2000||10:37 PM||||I have researched this a little more and I have found that the wrap just causes to many problems. The best way to reduce under hood temperatures is to go with something like Jet Hot ceramic coatings inside and out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||04-03-2000||08:26 AM||||I've driven the car from Atlanta to Sandestin Florida.. (6hrs) I rial on it nearly every friday and saturday night at the strip or at street lights. What problems is everyone having? Cause I spoke with the shop owner and he has had no problems with ceramic tape in the 15+years hes been in the business? There is a broken Kitty at the shop with a 350 in it and the hedman units have been wrapped on that car for nearly 40,000 miles with no ill-effects?!? (Broken Kitty = 84 Jaguar XJ-6L)I'm not arguing with ya i'm just wanting to know what going wrong? Jet Hot is the best way to go.. but Pricey! ||||reg||1
